message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal but complete example of an “interactive rotating card” that flips (rotates around its Y‑axis) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste this into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    margin: 0;
    height: 100vh;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    width:260px;          /* width of the card */
    height:360px;         /* height of the card */
    perspective:800px;   /* gives depth effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card itself (front & back) ---------- */
.card {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform .6s ease-in-out;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
}

.card:hover {                     /* rotate on hover */
    transform:rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front side ---------- */
.front, .back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;     /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.front img{
    max-width:80%;
    border-radius:8px;
    margin-bottom:15px;
}

.front h2{margin:0;font-size:1.5rem;color:#333;}
.front p{font-size:.9rem;color:#666;margin-top:10px;}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Back side ---------- */
.back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* start flipped */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.back h3{margin:0;font-size:1.4rem;color:#444;}
.back p{font-size:.95rem;color:#555;margin-top:8px;}
.back button{
    margin-top:15px;
    padding:.5em 1.2em;
    font-size:.9rem;
    color:#fff;
    background:#007bff;
    border:none;
    border-radius:4px;
    cursor:pointer;
}
.back button:hover{background:#0056b3;}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front face -->
        <div class="front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/200/140?random=1" alt="Sample image">
            <h2>Tytuł karty</h2>
            <p>Krótki opis lub teaser, który zachęca do przewrócenia.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back face -->
        <div class="back">
            <h3>Więcej informacji</h3>
            <p>Tu możesz dodać szczegółowe dane, linki, przyciski czy inne elementy interaktywne.</p>
            <button>Zobacz więcej</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper creates a 3‑D context. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3‑D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the reverse side when not visible. |
| **4** | On hover, the whole card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis (`rotateY`). |
| **5** | The back side is initially rotated 180°, so after the card’s rotation it becomes visible. |

Feel free to tweak sizes, colors, or add more content. Happy coding!
